Use native 64-bit off_t on musl Linux.

_linux.h only treats glibc as having large-file support. On musl that
defines _PR_NO_LARGE_FILES, so PR_Seek64 emulates lseek with a 2GiB
offset cap. Firefox uses PR_Seek64 for File.slice() during chunked
uploads, which then fail past 2GiB.

musl's off_t is always 64-bit, so _PR_HAVE_LARGE_OFF_T is the correct
feature set (same as BSD).
--- a/pr/include/md/_linux.h
+++ b/pr/include/md/_linux.h
@@ -336,7 +336,8 @@
     || defined(ANDROID)
 #define _PR_HAVE_OFF64_T
 #else
-#define _PR_NO_LARGE_FILES
+/* musl and other non-glibc Linux: off_t is already 64-bit. */
+#define _PR_HAVE_LARGE_OFF_T
 #endif
 #if (__GLIBC__ > 2) || (__GLIBC__ == 2 && __GLIBC_MINOR__ >= 1) \
     || defined(ANDROID)
